The user is asking a simple question: how many work-hours do I consider equivalent to one estimated workday, based on the previous estimation context. I should not revise, recalculate, or restate the previous effort estimate. Just return valid JSON with the number of work hours per workday.

Standard software development estimation often uses 8 work hours per workday (a standard full-time shift). Sometimes it's 6 or 7 for productive coding hours, but typically in project management, 1 workday = 8 work hours. I will use 8.

The schema requires:
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "work_hours_per_workday": {
      "type": "number",
      "exclusiveMinimum": 0
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "work_hours_per_workday"
  ]
}

So I will return:
{
  "work_hours_per_workday": 8
}

No other text, just valid JSON.

